<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:camunda="http://camunda.org/schema/1.0/bpmn" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:modeler="http://camunda.org/schema/modeler/1.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="Definitions_customerSnapshot" targetNamespace="http://example.com/bpmn" modeler:executionPlatform="Camunda Platform" modeler:executionPlatformVersion="7.24.0">
  <!--
    5 parallel GETs, each storing a different object (profile, contact, address, account, loyalty).
    The POST deep-merges all 5 (in the "sources" order - later wins) and builds the body
    from the inline body schema.
    Start variables: apiBaseUrl, customerId, accessToken (JWT, sent as Bearer on every call), initiator (optional)
  -->
  <bpmn:process id="customer-snapshot" name="Customer snapshot" isExecutable="true" camunda:historyTimeToLive="P30D">
    <bpmn:startEvent id="start" name="Snapshot requested">
      <bpmn:outgoing>toFork</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:parallelGateway id="fork" name="Fetch all">
      <bpmn:incoming>toFork</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>in_profile</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>in_contact</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>in_address</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>in_account</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>in_loyalty</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:parallelGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="getProfile" name="GET profile" camunda:delegateExpression="${restGet}">
      <bpmn:documentation>[REST connector] REST GET - Fetch data: request params built from the pasted OpenAPI parameters; 4xx -&gt; BPMN error HTTP_&lt;status&gt;.
Implementation: delegateExpression ${restGet}
Inputs (leave empty when not needed):
- url: Request URL. Supports ${expressions} and {placeholders} that are filled from params with "x-in": "path". Example: ${apiBaseUrl}/users/{userId}
- sources: Comma separated process variable names (or a JSON literal) deep-merged in order - later wins. Example: currentUser, userChanges
- paramsSchema: Paste the operation's "parameters" list from the service's OpenAPI / Swagger document (in: path | query | header). A parameter is filled from the merged sources, else from the process variable with the same name. Paste it as JSON or YAML (OpenAPI 3.x or Swagger 2.0); "$ref"s must resolve inside the pasted text, so paste the referenced components too, or the whole document plus a top-level "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Name". Add "x-source": "/json/pointer" or "x-expression": "varName" (no dollar-brace wrapper) where your process data is named differently. Long pastes (a whole OpenAPI document) work with history level activity or none; with audit / full history the engine stores every input in history and limits it to 4000 characters.
- headers: JSON object, values may use ${expressions}. Example: {"X-Correlation-Id": "${execution.processInstanceId}"}
- responseSchema: Optional. Paste the response schema from the service's OpenAPI / Swagger document: a schema object, a response, or the operation's "responses" (the first 2xx is used). Shapes the response (only declared properties are kept, writeOnly ones dropped) and validates it. Violation -&gt; BPMN error RESPONSE_INVALID. Paste it as JSON or YAML (OpenAPI 3.x or Swagger 2.0); "$ref"s must resolve inside the pasted text, so paste the referenced components too, or the whole document plus a top-level "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Name". Add "x-source": "/json/pointer" or "x-expression": "varName" (no dollar-brace wrapper) where your process data is named differently. Long pastes (a whole OpenAPI document) work with history level activity or none; with audit / full history the engine stores every input in history and limits it to 4000 characters.
- resultVariable: Process variable receiving the response body (stored as JSON).
- statusVariable: Process variable receiving the HTTP status code.
- technicalErrors: exception (default): the task fails - incident, or retried with async before. bpmnError: thrown as BPMN error HTTP_5xx / CONNECTION_FAILED so an error boundary event or error event subprocess can handle it. 4xx (HTTP_4xx) and schema errors (REQUEST_INVALID / RESPONSE_INVALID) are always BPMN errors.
- mockEnabled: Test mode: true = do not send the request, answer with Mock status / Mock response instead (the request is still built and validated, the response schema, error mapping and result variables work as for a real call). false or empty = real call. An expression switches it per instance, e.g. ${execution.getVariable('useMockData') == true}.
- mockStatus: HTTP status the mock answers with (default 200). A 4xx / 5xx tests the error handling, e.g. 404 -&gt; BPMN error HTTP_404.
- mockResponse: Response body the mock answers with: a JSON object / array (or text); empty = no body. ${expressions} inside are evaluated by the engine, so the mock can echo process variables.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <camunda:inputOutput>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="url">${apiBaseUrl}/customers/{customerId}/profile</camunda:inputParameter>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="sources" />
          <camunda:inputParameter name="paramsSchema">- name: customerId
  in: path
  required: true
  schema:
    type: integer
    minimum: 1</camunda:inputParameter>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="headers" />
          <camunda:inputParameter name="responseSchema" />
          <camunda:inputParameter name="resultVariable">profile</camunda:inputParameter>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="statusVariable" />
          <camunda:inputParameter name="technicalErrors">bpmnError</camunda:inputParameter>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="mockEnabled">${execution.getVariable('useMockData') == true}</camunda:inputParameter>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="mockStatus">200</camunda:inputParameter>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="mockResponse">{
  "customer": {
    "id": 501,
    "firstName": "Noa",
    "lastName": "Levi",
    "birthDate": "1990-04-12",
    "internalNotes": "vip"
  },
  "_links": {
    "self": "/api/customers/501/profile"
  }
}</camunda:inputParameter>
        </camunda:inputOutput>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>in_profile</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>out_profile</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="getContact" name="GET contact" camunda:delegateExpression="${restGet}">
      <bpmn:documentation>[REST connector] REST GET - Fetch data: request params built from the pasted OpenAPI parameters; 4xx -&gt; BPMN error HTTP_&lt;status&gt;.
